$Id: NEWS,v 1.26 2010/05/07 19:08:25 kamada Exp $

2026-09-08 Derek Moore

	* IP_ANY is IP_RW for SA endpoints and SPD: skip static mixed-family
	  tmpl (c0a8:444f::); install policy from the live IKE address.
	  if_xfrm coerce unspecified side; refuse mixed concrete families.
	* RFC 4555 MOBIKE responder: N(MOBIKE_SUPPORTED) in IKE_AUTH,
	  UPDATE_SA_ADDRESSES → XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE + IKE/Child endpoints.
	  iPhone is a roaming peer. Matrix ikev2-netns-mobike is the knob,
	  not a roam proof.
	* MOBIKE migrate uses the CP lease as the inner selector (not conf
	  PEERS_NET), inbound+FWD tmpl peer→local, XFRMA_ENCAP new NAT-T
	  ports. Kernel ENOENT left ESP on the old outer after roam.
	* Linux FWD clone snapshots inbound selector+tmpl before
	  rcpfk_handler; otherwise FWD becomes LAN→CP and SSH to other
	  LAN hosts misses (ping to the box still works).
	* Child PFS and IKE_SA rekey DH: oakley_dh_gencmp_submit /
	  oakley_dh_generate_submit → crypto_job_submit (N=0 inlines).
	* Matrix: xfrm-tmpl-family; ikev1-strongswan unskipped (netns
	  negotiation+SAD, same shape as ikev2).

	* int/gsoc2026: 3-way merge of linux-km + origin/gsoc2026.
	  iPhone IKEv2 NAT-T ping/SSH proven on this branch
	  (AES-CBC + hmac-sha256 ICV128, espinudp).
	* Frag reassembly (CVE-2016-10396 class): 60s timeout, max 4
	  assemblies/SA, 64k cap on IKEv2 SKF and IKEv1 FRAG.

2026-09-07 Derek Moore

	* nat_traversal is three-state: off / on (detect, default) /
	  force. force zeros NAT-D (RFC 3947 mismatch => both ends
	  encapsulate), sets NAT_DETECTED/behind_nat, floats 4500,
	  ESPINUDP. Same knob on IKEv1 and IKEv2. Grammar:
	  `nat_traversal force;`
	* Linux IKE bypass: UDP 500/4500 same-port and 500<->4500
	  float (RFC 3947) in spmd, not the matrix harness.
	* Transport SADB: copy endpoints, snapshot encap ports, then
	  selector ports 0. IKEv1 and IKEv2 Child.
	* RFC 3947 NAT-OA on XFRM: sa_natoa_* → XFRMA_ENCAP encap_oa.
	  lib/xfrmnatt + matrix row xfrm-natt-oa (root). IKEv1 fills
	  oa whenever ph1_wants_espinudp, not only NAT_DETECTED.
	* ubuntu.yml / netbsd.yml fire on int/gsoc2026 as well as
	  linux-km. Matrix: ikev2-netns-frag (RFC 7383 knob; not a
	  reassembly proof).
	* ikev2_frag.c: 3-arg ikev2_encrypt + AEAD AAD; SKF ICV inside
	  payload_length like SK. IKEv2 transport SADB zeros a copy
	  (IP_RW/NULL config must not mutate parent IKE ports).

2026-09-06 Derek Moore

	* Linux default KM is NETLINK_XFRM (`--with-km-backend=xfrm`).
	  Linux AF_KEY drops kernel→user datagrams on rcvbuf (no
	  netlink_overrun); not the default. BSD stays pfkey.
	  `--with-km-backend=pfkey` still builds if_pfkeyv2.c.
	* samples/upnp_portmap.py: this IGD SOAP AddPortMapping is
	  Action Failed; Windows HNetCfg.NATUPnP maps UDP 500/4500
	  (lease 0) and NAT-PMP also works. 500 is not reserved-blocked.
	* samples/linux-matrix: WSL case-row harness (unit, admin-empty,
	  ikev2-netns workers=0 and workers=1, skip ikev1-strongswan).
	  Numeric workers cell relaunches iked -F with
	  RACOON2_CRYPTO_WORKERS. Does not enable racoon2.target.
	* lib/if_xfrm.c: always emit XFRMA_ALG_AUTH_TRUNC. The #ifdef guard
	  was dead — XFRMA_ALG_AUTH_TRUNC is an enum, not a #define — so
	  every ESP SA fell back to plain XFRMA_ALG_AUTH and Linux used a
	  96-bit ICV for hmac(sha256). RFC 4868 peers (Apple, strongSwan)
	  send 128 bits; the ICV mismatch ate every packet
	  (XfrmInStateProtoError, 0 InNoStates). Live: iPhone espinudp
	  tunnel now AES-CBC + hmac(sha256)-128 bits, pings both ways.
	* ikev2: IKE_SA DH generate/compute goes through
	  oakley_dh_*_submit → crypto_job_submit (N=0 inlines).
	  CREATE_CHILD PFS and IKEv1 ident use oakley_dh_gencmp_submit.
	* spmd: unlink spmif only after LISTEN_FDS miss, before bind.
	  Unlink-before-take dropped the name iked connect()s to.
	* admin: establish-sa/vpn-connect surface errno (ENOENT if no
	  selector). ikedctl masks ADMIN_FLAG_LONG_REPLY before
	  ac_errno (aliases ac_len_high). reload-config is SIGHUP
	  (ikev2_shutdown then reread).

2026-09-05 Derek Moore

	* lib: Linux NETLINK_XFRM SAD/SPD backend
	  (lib/if_xfrm.c), XOR-compiled with if_pfkeyv2.c via
	  --with-km-backend=xfrm|pfkey. Linux default is xfrm
	  (2026-09-06); AF_KEY is opt-in.
	* samples: Linux systemd units (spmd/iked/kinkd) with
	  ProtectSystem=strict, PrivateTmp, and socket activation.
	  spmd.socket is /run/racoon2/spmif; iked.socket is UDP
	  500/4500. LISTEN_FDS helper in lib/sd_listenfds.c (no
	  libsystemd). Default startup_scripts on Linux is systemd.
	* iked: Linux default event wait is epoll (--disable-epoll for
	  select). Crypto worker pool (--with-crypto-workers=N or
	  RACOON2_CRYPTO_WORKERS, default 0) with main-thread drain via
	  pipe. OpenSSL 3 providers (--with-openssl-provider=NAME or
	  RACOON2_OPENSSL_PROVIDER) and ENGINE
	  (--with-openssl-engine=ID / RACOON2_OPENSSL_ENGINE).
	  oakley_dh_* is not enqueued yet. make check: evlooptest,
	  workerstest (beside eaytest).
	* lib: userspace SAD/SPD backend (lib/if_userspace.c), XOR
	  --with-km-backend=userspace. Loopback socketpair drives
	  iked GETSPI/UPDATE callbacks; optional unix datagram to
	  RACOON2_DATAPLANE_SOCK. No DPDK app, no XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV.
	  make check: kmtest (compiles if_userspace.c even when KM is pfkey).
	* ESP AES-GCM-16 (RFC 4106): config aes_gcm, XFRMA_ALG_AEAD
	  rfc4106(gcm(aes)). Pair with non_auth.
	* Autoconf 2.71 (Ubuntu 24.04). AC_PREREQ 2.13 generated a
	  broken configure on 2.71 (m4sh functions after option
	  parse; lib NAT-T AC_EGREP_CPP ate AC_FUNC_MEMCMP).
	* kinkd: MIT krb5 1.20 dropped krb5_rc_close/resolve_full;
	  use krb5_get_server_rcache + krb5_rc_destroy. GCC 10
	  -fno-common: rcf_interface_head is extern in kink_conf.h.
	* eaytest DH: exponent length 0 (matches oakley gen2). OpenSSL 3
	  rejects a 96-bit secret vs a 1536-bit p; generate retries
	  without DH_set_length if the first call fails.
	* eaytest DES/3DES: OpenSSL 3 DES_key_sched rejects even-parity
	  keys; use DES_set_key_unchecked. Cipher vector radix is 16.
	  eaytest honors RACOON2_OPENSSL_PROVIDER / RACOON2_OPENSSL_ENGINE
	  like iked (AFALG ENGINE vs default AES-NI).
	* samples/macos_ikev2.conf: IKEv2 PSK road-warrior for macOS 26/27
	  (AES-CBC IKE, ESP GCM-16 then AES-CBC+SHA2-256, DH14/15).
	  Client steps: doc/macos-26-27-ikev2-client.md
	* iked: bind IKE when IPSEC_POLICY bypass is unsupported.
	  Linux/WSL IP_IPSEC_POLICY is EOPNOTSUPP; still bind UDP 500/4500.
	* iked: RFC 5282 AES-GCM-16 on the IKE Encrypted Payload (AAD is
	  IKE header through Encrypted Payload header). kmp_enc_alg
	  { aes_gcm; } with kmp_hash_alg { non_auth; } omits INTEGR.
	  ESP GCM is still RFC 4106.
	* lib/if_xfrm.c: do not store XFRM_INF in add/use expire seconds.
	  Kernel `if (hard_use_expires_seconds)` treats ~0ULL as signed −1
	  and hard-expires the SA in ~1s (XfrmInNoStates). 0 = unlimited,
	  matching iproute2. Byte/packet limits still use XFRM_INF.
	* lib/if_xfrm.c: XFRMA_ENCAP only when rcpfk_msg.natt_type is set.
	  Port 4500 on the IKE sockaddr is not NAT. iked sets natt_type
	  from behind_nat / peer_behind_nat; IKEv1 sets it from
	  NAT_DETECTED (pfkey.c update/add).
	* lib/cfsetup.c: rcf_get_rvrs_selector skips same direction
	  (0.0.0.0/0 matched itself → spmd 550, no SPD).
	* spmd: POLICY ADD uses urgent SPDUPDATE so XFRM ACK is not
	  overwritten by a second pending FWD.
	* spmd: Linux IKE UDP 500/4500 XFRM allow policies before tunnel
	  SPD (IP_IPSEC_POLICY is EOPNOTSUPP). Any SAMODE; cached per
	  endpoint pair, failures logged.
	* samples/upnp_portmap.py: UPnP IGD mapping for IKE UDP 500 /
	  4500 to this host (miniupnpc). Router IGDs that refuse
	  AddPortMapping (Action Failed) need a manual forward.
	* Linux: ikedctl unix admin (`--enable-admin`, default).
	  show-sa/flush-sa/establish-sa/vpn-connect isakmp via
	  /var/run/iked.sock. Kernel SAD/SPD remains `ip xfrm`.
	  T4 admin_reply send loop (EINTR/short write). Do not
	  XOR-compile ikedctl for netlink.

2020-02-05 Christos Zoulas, Chuck Zmudzinski

	* begin testing racoon2 as L2TP/IPsec or IKEv2 VPN server on
	  Linux for compatability with built-in Windows, iOS, and Android
	  VPN clients
	* IKEv1 L2TP/IPsec VPN connections from built-in Windows 10 and
	  iOS 13 VPN clients to racoon2 VPN server on Linux successfully
	  tested
	* successfully tested multiple simultaneous L2TP/IPsec or IKEv2
	  connections from built-in Windows or Apple VPN clients to racoon2
	  on NetBSD and multiple simultaneous L2TP/IPsec connections from
	  built-in Windows or Apple VPN clients to racoon2 on Linux
	* limited support for IKEv2 VPN connections from Windows 10 to
	  racoon2 VPN server on Linux successfully tested - due to
	  limitations of the pfkeyv2 interface to the Linux kernel that
	  racoon2 uses, only IKEv2 IPv4 in IPv4 tunnels have been
	  successfully tested usign racoon2 on Linux. It is likely IPv6 in
	  IPv6 tunnels will also work on Linux, but this has not been tested
	  yet. IPv6 in IPv4 tunnels are not compatable with the current
	  version of racoon2 on Linux
	* begin evaluating approaches to extend the capabilities of racoon2
	  on Linux

